Description: n900: announce the info server again after every modem reset
 n900_pre_sim() runs again whenever the modem comes back after a reset and
 created a new PN_EPOC_INFO server on top of the old one. gisi sends
 PNS_NAME_ADD_REQ only for the first handler bound to a resource, so after
 the first modem reset the name was never announced again, while the
 modem's name service had forgotten it in the reset. When the radio came
 on (MTC_NORMAL) the modem found nobody to answer its
 INFO_SERIAL_NUMBER_READ_REQ (IMEISV for the network) and reset itself
 about two seconds later, every time: on the Nokia N950 the modem never
 stayed online. Harmattan's csd answers that request. Destroy the old
 server before creating the new one (which deregisters and registers the
 name again), and in n900_remove().
 .
 Found on the N950: with the name registered and the request answered by
 hand, the modem stayed online; without it, it reset after MTC_NORMAL
 even with no other ISI traffic.
Author: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-10
---
--- a/plugins/n900.c	2026-11-10 22:31:20.006284388 +0100
+++ b/plugins/n900.c	2026-11-10 22:31:20.015364809 +0100
@@ -386,6 +386,7 @@
 	if (isi->timeout)
 		g_source_remove(isi->timeout);
 
+	isi_infoserver_destroy(isi->infoserver);
 	g_isi_client_destroy(isi->client);
 	g_isi_modem_destroy(isi->modem);
 	g_free(isi);
@@ -464,6 +465,16 @@
 
 	DBG("(%p) with %s", modem, isi->ifname);
 
+	/*
+	 * pre_sim runs again after every modem reset. The modem's name
+	 * service forgets PN_EPOC_INFO in the reset, and gisi announces a
+	 * server's name only when its first handler is bound: a second
+	 * infoserver on top of the old one never announced it again. The
+	 * modem then got no answer to its serial number (IMEISV) query when
+	 * the radio came on and reset itself, over and over (Nokia N950).
+	 * Drop the old server first so the name is announced afresh.
+	 */
+	isi_infoserver_destroy(isi->infoserver);
 	isi->infoserver = isi_infoserver_create(modem, isi->modem);
 
 	ofono_sim_create(modem, 0, "isimodem", isi->modem);
